node_modules
# A bare `node_modules` only matches the root one — Docker does not apply it to
# nested paths. The deploy images install dependencies BEFORE copying source, so
# a workspace's own node_modules riding in from the build context would land on
# top of the installed tree and corrupt pnpm's links. It also keeps the context
# small.
**/node_modules
.git
.turbo
**/.next
**/dist
coverage
logs
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
**/.env
**/.env.local
deploy/.env
.cursor
.trash
.claude
agent-transcripts
**/.DS_Store
supabase/.temp
